module Main
import Base
import Borrow
-- Containment (spec 2026-08-10), full-branch review round: the RESULT of a
-- projection, record literal, or record extension is judged by its own type.
--
-- The BASE of a projection/extension is an allowed position, so that reading an
-- ordinary field (`r.n`) stays legal when a SIBLING field holds a carrier. That
-- allowance left the carrier reachable one keystroke from the rejected
-- `leak r = [r]`, via four spellings that are all this same escape:
--
--     [r.b]                    -- the raw Borrow, in a list
--     [R { ..r, n = 1 }]       -- same Borrow, new record
--     [R { b = r.b, n = 1 }]   -- same Borrow, rebuilt field-by-field
--     [p.h]                    -- an effect handle out of its `with` scope
--
-- All four are now rejected by judging the node's RESULT type, which is what
-- distinguishes them from `r.n : U64` (not a carrier, still legal).
--
-- This file pins the extension form. `bump` was briefly an ACCEPT fixture,
-- which pinned record-return escape as correct and contradicted the sibling
-- `leak r = [r]` reject in carrier-field-record.wok -- one keystroke apart, the
-- opposite verdict.
data R = R { b : Borrow, n : U64 }
bump : R -> R
bump r = R { ..r, n = 1 }
main : U64
main = 0
